{"boundary":"Configured source-text signatures, not elaborated Lean or a complete dependency context. Truncation and unresolved names are explicit; full definitions and source remain on demand.","contributions":[{"author":{"kind":"agent","name":"Codex source review 1"},"body":"The captured configured assertion and the cited paper assertion were read with their relevant definitions; the disclosed relation follows the stated scope, not the previous frontend choice.\n\nInspected: Read all three declarations, T12 Sobolev-Fourier representation, finite maximal lifespan and pointwise self-similar blowup limit, together with the Gaussian coefficient law.","content_sha256":"sha256:8066437cc9f5aad34448ac5dbe6bedddf04dcd6c615ca5298a835307f2c7befa","fingerprint":"sha256:d98282e1241d7e441e170237f9cbd0e6ea9b42eb7ae5517bb3260f753c5dd614","kind":"statement-link","license":"Apache-2.0","navigation":{"decision":"linked","limitations":"Agent source reading; no human approval, Lean replay or whole-statement equivalence certificate. The captured configured assertion and the cited paper assertion were read with their relevant definitions; the disclosed relation follows the stated scope, not the previous frontend choice.","schema":"statement-map-navigation-reading/1","source_sha256":"sha256:0804a85c29daa715ecb378d4a0dbcf233429b187648c068199775fd067c1bf9c","targets":[{"declarations":["OAI.DefocusingNLS.stable_blowup"],"explanation":"The stable-blowup declaration chooses arbitrarily large odd powers and a Sobolev index k>8 with a nonempty open set of initial data on the twelve-dimensional torus exhibiting finite-time self-similar blowup. The paper’s theorem states the same open-set phenomenon with power chosen sufficiently large and exponent 1/(p−1).","fingerprint":"sha256:5b7428c6934ccb4b3b4248ae999e0e91d88454cd9a36adf2783120bed01adb83","limitations":"The Sobolev/Fourier presentation and maximal-flow definitions were read at their source boundary, not independently verified.","relation":"